Data Wrangling

cafe_english &lt;- cafe |&gt;
1  filter(country %in% c("Australia", "USA", "UK"))

cafe_summary &lt;- cafe_english |&gt;
  group_by(country) |&gt;
2  summarize(mean = mean(price_gbp), median = median(price_gbp)) |&gt;
3  pivot_longer(-country, names_to="summary") |&gt;
  mutate(summary = factor(summary))


1

Get only the UK, US, and Australia

2

Summarize price_gbp, getting the median and mean

3

Pivot longer, so that we have long-form data with the summary name as the column name. This makes plotting easier.
